Each one contains structured knowledge that powers the
Bashcrawl help system.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
⚡ EXPLORING THE SCRIPTORIUM
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Use 'ls' to see the contents of this chamber:

    ls

You will find shell scripts (.sh) and a data/ directory
containing YAML knowledge tablets.

To read the structured data:

    cat data/commands.yaml      Command reference data
    cat data/map.yaml           The dungeon map data
    cat data/quests.yaml        Quest definitions
    cat data/rooms.yaml         Room descriptions

To read the help engine itself:

    cat bashcrawl_help.sh       The main help engine
    cat command_suggester.sh    Context-aware suggestions
    cat ai_engine.sh            Player pattern analysis

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
⚡ ACTIVATING THE HELP SYSTEM
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

To permanently activate the help system in your current
terminal session, source the initialization script using
the full path (since you arrived here through a portal):

    source $BASHCRAWL_ROOT/src/help/init_help.sh

If BASHCRAWL_ROOT is not set, find your game root first:

    BASHCRAWL_ROOT=$(cd -P "$(dirname "$(readlink portal)")"/../.. && pwd)
    source $BASHCRAWL_ROOT/src/help/init_help.sh

This will:
  - Define the 'help' command as a shell function
  - Export BASHCRAWL_ROOT so spells know where home is
  - Enable context-aware help from any room

After sourcing, try these from any room in the dungeon:

    help                     Location-aware guidance
    help commands            Full command reference
    help map                 The dungeon map

